#image("kernels-101.svg", width: 100%)

*Seed 101.* The original persistent search kernel is the largest trace row.
The GPU had a kernel active for 99.1% of the span between its first kernel
start and last kernel end. This is kernel coverage, not measured SM utilization.
Launch gaps are small within this trace. One-time table construction is included,
so its setup/query shares must not be transferred to a full recovery run.

*Copies.* The host cudaMemcpy API total includes waiting for the search result.
The GPU memory trace for seed101 records only 0.033888 ms device-to-host and
0.000736 ms host-to-device; API wait time is not bulk-transfer cost.

