#image("kernels-202.svg", width: 100%)

*Seed 202.* Kernel coverage was 98.7%. Table preparation occupies a larger
fraction of this eight-query trace than for seed101. These profiler durations
are diagnostic values, not production throughput or a cross-host comparison.

*Hardware counters.* Both Nsight Compute attempts returned unsupported with
ERR_NVGPUCTRPERM. The separate probe built, ran and checked its control kernel,
but encountered the same provider counter restriction. No hardware instruction,
occupancy or warp-stall counters were collected or estimated. No driver setting
was changed. The block-clock results from v1 remain separately preserved.

*Accounting.* Six planned process attempts: two unprofiled exact-reply successes,
two successful timelines, two unsupported counter attempts. The capability probe
is separate. Native summaries, SVGs and report sources regenerated byte-identically.
Canonical export/schema/coverage/file checks passed with zero findings. The owned
pod fmu20lo21ib6gu was deleted and absence verified; the v1 pod was already gone.

*Reproduction.* CUDA 13.2 pinned image; Nsight Systems 2025.6.3 and Compute 2026.1.1,
installed via pinned 13.2.2 metapackages. The launch manifest hashes bash; the actual
GPU service hash is in instruments.sha256. Source b50e30d47458881eba10d802b7f972a9f56541bd.
Protocol SHA256: 4dc4c0560a8af2ad967d99c9f1d08526eb676e435b12ef658a174e093eba869e.
Study: research/explicit_relations_profile_20261031; raw results-v2/export.json.

